## Conversation
The user requested the planned Mooncake Store shared-cache routing implementation and then requested separate logical commits. The feature must provide conservative optional cache hints while preserving admission, GPU overlap, scheduler selection, cached-token accounting, and HiCache behavior.

## Actions
Implemented strict contract validation, exact object/prefix/medium residency, learned identity edges, sequence and generation fencing, bounded state, and full-attention, sliding-window, and Mamba-align readiness. Integrated admission-scoped metadata watches, passive per-router ownership, delayed subscriber startup, local primary Stored observation, exact precomputed hash-slice reuse, positive frontend request eligibility, and opt-in configuration. Added both-indexer oracle, eligibility, scoring, watch, and task-lifecycle coverage. Final complete-tree validation passed 963 router-core tests and 189 integrated LLM tests with 2 and 3 ignored respectively. Rust configuration passed 44 tests; Python configuration passed 81 using a package-initializer bypass. Bindings and consumer compilation, formatting, whitespace, and targeted Clippy checks passed. Intermediate commits were not built separately.

## Errors & Mistakes
A remote-indexer configuration regression first failed because deserialization did not validate the new option. Other compile failures included Option handling, range integer types, and a required KvIndexerInterface test-utility import removed from the wrong scope. An exact exported key prefix containing @ but missing its digest initially produced a false hit; the red regression passed after checking exact-prefix malformed keys before splitting. Old-generation batches and malformed frames initially lacked complete successor-state fencing. An existing recovery test timed out in the parallel run, then passed alone and in the final serial run; no underlying timeout cause was established. Commit preparation rejected one overlong body line with body's lines must not be longer than 100 characters [body-max-line-length]; the shorter message passed the validator.

## Dead Ends
An endpoint-wide strong cache map would violate router lifetime ownership. Looking up runtime metadata for every request would add unnecessary hot-path work. Prefix-monotonic stopping and rounding down a later hybrid hit are unsound for sliding-window or Mamba state. The implementation instead validates changed snapshots, traverses learned identities once, and proves each candidate endpoint. An early consumer compile command disabled required benchmark features; the corrected feature set passed.

## Hints for Future Agents
Runtime metadata is excluded from MDC checksum equality, so validate optional contracts against admitted membership separately. Pending or closed watches must withhold observation and queries. try_lock in the pending callback avoids lock inversion. Preserve identity quarantine and sequence across residency invalidation. Require every exported parallel prefix and keep CPU and disk medium bits independent. Sequence gaps clear residency before accepting a batch. Stale generations must neither clear successor state nor advance its cursor. Shared hits are one logical proven prefix, not physical object counts or cached-token credits.

## Codebase Discoveries
Normalized GPU integer hashes expose only low 64 bits while store keys retain full SHA-256 digests. Useful supported geometry includes FA32 plus SWA8/window8, but not SWA8/window16. The final three-group TP2 debug benchmark averaged 8422.0 microseconds for 4096 blocks and 39280.4 microseconds for 16384 blocks over 32 runs each. Measured backing-map allocations at fixed caps were about 98.5 MiB live and 117 MiB during growth; these are not process RSS or total cache memory.

## Open Questions
Initialized pinned-connector, live Mooncake, and GPU acceptance remain unverified. GPU coverage must include TP at least 2 with full-attention plus sliding-window and full-attention plus Mamba, useful reuse after GPU eviction, and a miss when one required parallel object is absent. Silent reconnects and lost final removal events remain best-effort staleness limits. The Python configuration bypass is not native binding integration validation.
